row(4, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE LORD WAS ANGRY WITH ME ON YOUR ACCOUNT AND SWORE THAT I SHOULD NOT CROSS THE JORDAN NOR COME INTO THE GOOD LAND THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU FOR AN INHERITANCE — THE THIRD TELLING OF THE BAR. {HP(4, 21, (("ויהוה", "התאנף", "בי", "על", "דבריכם"), "and the LORD WAS ANGRY with me ON YOUR ACCOUNT — 1:37\'s wrath-verb (the hitpael\'s fourteen seats; 1:37, 4:21, 9:8, 9:20 the Torah\'s) where 3:26 wrote \'was wroth\'; \'on your account\' one seat against 1:37\'s \'for your sakes\' (Micah 3:12 its other) (computed)"), (("וישבע", "לבלתי", "עברי", "את", "הירדן"), "and SWORE that I should not cross the Jordan — the oath here alone of the three tellings; one seat (computed)"), (("ולבלתי", "בא", "אל", "הארץ", "הטובה"), "nor come into the good land — one seat; \'the good land\' five seats in the book (1:35, 3:25, 4:21, 4:22, 9:6) (computed)"))} → {AP(4, 21, (("ומן", "קדם", "יי", "הוה", "רגז", "עלי"), "and FROM BEFORE the LORD there was anger against me — the phrase\'s fourteen seats, 1:37 and 3:26 among them (computed)"), (("וקיים", "בדיל", "דלא", "למעבר"), "and he SWORE that I should not cross — \'swore\' one seat (computed)"))} THE READBACK: 1:37 (\'for your sakes\', the ground OPEN at 1b against Numbers 20:12), 3:26 (\'for your sakes\', the plea refused), 4:21 (\'on your account\', an OATH) — three tellings, three grounds: the disagreement row of 1b widens by one; the diff against Numbers 20:12 shares \'with me\', \'the land\', \'which\' (computed).')
